WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.922
A machine learning model should be compared with a simple reference point.

00:00:03.922 --> 00:00:10.222
The DummyClassifier uses a basic strategy: always predict the most frequent class.

00:00:10.222 --> 00:00:14.467
That gives us baseline accuracy with almost no intelligence.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:18.334
Logistic regression is then evaluated on the same test data.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:26.842
If a more complex model cannot beat a simple baseline, we should question whether the model adds useful predictive

00:00:26.842 --> 00:00:30.782
value. Baselines help put performance numbers into context.
